This is a small Pluxel monorepo with one deployable `web` workspace, one plugin and one
framework-neutral domain package. Start with plugin behavior; host composition is documented
separately below.

## Develop the plugin

Before changing `plugins/`, contracts, host policy or lint configuration, read
[`docs/pluxel/README.md`](docs/pluxel/README.md). `pluxel new` copies that documentation verbatim
from the `user-docs/` bundled with the CLI, so the generated repository uses the same authoring,
testing and Oxlint guidance as Pluxel itself. Coding agents are directed there by `AGENTS.md`.

The main plugin is `plugins/example/src/index.ts`. Its test uses `@pluxel/test/vitest` and
`withRuntimeHost()` to prove that business HTTP works with Workbench Plane disabled. Keep that
property as the plugin grows.

Run the complete local verification before finishing a change:

```sh
pnpm lint:fix
pnpm verify
```

`verify` checks format, unused lint suppressions, types, tests and the production build. Treat
Pluxel rule failures as ownership or correctness feedback; do not broadly disable them.
Workspace build, test and typecheck tasks run through Turborepo. Pure builds can use all logical
CPUs; tests and combined verification reserve half of the Turbo slots for Vitest's own worker pool.
Results are stored in `.turbo`, so an unchanged second `pnpm verify` restores build outputs and skips
successful checks. Use `pnpm test:full` or `pnpm build:full` when you intentionally need to bypass
the cache, or lower `--concurrency` further on a memory-constrained machine.

## Start the application

```sh
pnpm install
pnpm dev
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:3310` for the typed GQLens greeting UI. Verify the underlying plugin business
route directly:

```sh
curl http://127.0.0.1:3310/__pluxel/plugins/{{className}}Plugin/api/greeting
```

## Project boundaries

- `web`: deployable Vite application, static host policy and React/GQLens frontend.
- `plugins/example`: plugin lifecycle, configuration and business HTTP routes.
- `packages/domain`: neutral logic shared by `web` and the plugin.

The repository root only coordinates workspaces, the pnpm version catalog, Turbo task graph and
shared quality tooling. Every workspace still declares every package it imports: `catalog:`
centralizes external versions but does not make a dependency implicitly available. `web/package.json` owns React,
GQLens, Vite and static runtime dependencies. Pluxel packages are catalog-managed registry
dependencies; only packages owned here use `workspace:*`. If the repository gains multiple
deployable applications, move `web` under an `apps/*` convention then.

## Host composition

The Vite plugin order in `web/vite.config.ts` is intentional:

1. Pluxel mounts the static runtime and plugin HTTP routes.
2. GQLens watches the domain schema and regenerates typed frontend accessors.
3. React provides normal component HMR.

GQLens middleware stays disabled because GraphQL is served by the Pluxel plugin, not by a second
development-only backend.

To enable the optional Pluxel Workbench, start with `PLUXEL_WORKBENCH=true`. The production build
uses the same `web/src/pluxel.static.ts` entry through `@pluxel/rolldown/build`; `web/dist` contains
the server closure, deployment manifest, browser application and Workbench artifacts and can be
moved as one directory. Plugin business routes and domain state must remain independent of that
capability.
